00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:10.530 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  today we would like to present an  example of a joint effort in the field  of justice reform and modernization  at the heart of this project is an  effort to modernize the existing rules  of civil procedure which have undergone  a serious reformation for the first time  in 60 years  since 2016 the cypriot authorities  notably the supreme court of cyprus have  been implementing a significant and  complex reform of the court system  this process is supported by the  european commission and the council of  europe  [Music]  the severe backlog of cases in cypriot  courts  made it clear that something had to be  done  as the justice system was going to  collapse and could no longer meet the  needs of the economy and society  as a result the supreme court in a  report in 2016  codified the functional problems of the  courts and managed to secure technical  assistance from the european commission  for an overall judicial reform one of  the projects undertaken was the revision  of the civil procedure rules  this is one of the most complex and  technical projects that i was called to  manage  [Music]  the european commission through dg  reform the directorate general for  structural reforms provided technical  support assistance through various  projects to the cypriot authorities and  to the supreme court this was in the  context of this important and complex  judicial reform  the commission provided support in two  consecutive phases mobilizing different  group of experts to advise and assist  the supreme court in this endeavor we  had a very good result the main result  of this common and highly successful  effort is the modernization of the civil  procedure rules the cooperation  consisted of several elements  one reviewing the old cypriot civil  procedure rules  two supporting in carrying out public  consultations three providing technical  inputs for the preparation of the text  of the new rules and four and final  communicating on the new rules  according to the eu justice scoreboard  cyprus was repeatedly encouraged to  improve its performance in terms of  length of court proceedings and level of  backlogs in civil and commercial cases  the modernization of the civil procedure  rules should support this improvement  the eu justice scoreboard provides  comparable data on the independence  quality and efficiency of national  justice systems  it mainly focuses on civil commercial  and administrative cases  to pave the way for a more investment  business  and citizen friendly environment  [Music]  the new civil procedure rules constitute  a new modern approach to core  proceedings they provide for new code  management powers orientated on  efficiency and timely adjudication the  principle of overriding objective  constitutes the cornerstone in the new  civil process enabling the court to deal  with cases justly and a proportionate  cost this is an important development in  the work of domestic courts in line with  fair trial and rule of law standards  [Music]  this change  certainly represents a challenge  but we are ready and waited for these  changes that can lead to the upgrading  of our profession  we are looking forward to new  efficient and fast court proceedings  advocates will need to adapt to the  management of the procedure by judges  the new rules will also provide new  fields of work especially in mediation  and arbitration as a result of the need  to follow pre-action protocols and the  powers of the court to refer issues to  these adr mechanisms  [Music]  we are very happy to be able to  contribute to the judicial reform in  cyprus we do this with this project  a joint project of the council of europe  and the european union  which is successful  thanks to the commitment and the  dedication of the cypriot authorities  this project is also a very good example  of the cooperation and complementarity  of the european union and the council of  europe two organizations that are based  on the same values of protecting human  rights and the rule of law  the adoption of the new rules on  civil procedure in cyprus is a very  important step in the development of the  justice reform a reform which is  essential  for the mutual trust for the trust of  citizens to democratic institutions  and for the  economic growth of the country  today the european commission continues  cooperating with the cypriot authorities  and together with the council of europe  prepare the ground for implementation  through training activities for judges  lawyers and court registrars the  implementation of the new rules will  contribute to a fairer and more  efficient justice system for everyone  [Music]  you

